3237:- Do not run full `PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -m pytest` “by inertia” before classifying the narrow runtime path: it exposed an unrelated embedding failure and consumed time/tokens. Do not broad-reset this dirty checkout; restore only explicitly classified files/hunks and preserve user changes. `provider_replay_blocked` is deliberate fail-closed behavior. [Task 5]
3239:- Green static tests from intermediate worktrees are not production proof. The recorded verdict is `NOT READY FOR PRODUCTION`: require authoritative diff → scope decision on shared queue → minimal OSINT deadline → one full test → clean commit → Railway sandbox OSINT-OFF regression → ON canary → burst/capacity evidence before controlled rollout. [Task 6]
3368:- Implementation commit `ebd5e81c11191d7fa45b1e8a48e25a487c2837fc` restored one `Упаковка и маркировка` stage with standard printing, marking, and WB order stickers; `npm run build`, `npm run test:unit` (115 tests), and targeted ESLint passed. Railway `web` and `WMS` reached `SUCCESS` at that SHA after pushing the Railway-tracked branch; full repository lint retained unrelated pre-existing failures. [Task 4]
3669:- Discovery receives a neutral minimal submission card, not cockpit, to avoid anchoring. Its lanes are risk identity/currentness, hidden obligations/costs, and BI/CBI bottlenecks; the final model cross-checks full LlamaParse JSON and cockpit. The prior experiment found 15/15 benchmark facts with three lanes versus 13/15 with one prompt. [Task 1]
3683:- Removing strict structured output to preserve provider citations let `hidden_obligations` return plain text. Use a citation-preserving structured-output contract; do not replay a full paid run for one failed lane when no single-lane endpoint exists without explicit approval. [Task 3]
